---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
      <main>
      	<h1>👾 Welcome to Mico</h1>
      
      	<p>
      		Mico is a Discord bot built as an experimental sandbox for OORTSKY, designed to prototype,
      		test, and evolve ideas directly in real usage environments.
      	</p>
      
      	<p>
      		Instead of being a static feature set, Mico functions as a living system where modules are
      		continuously iterated, refined, and sometimes replaced as better approaches emerge.
      	</p>
      
      	<p>Mico operates across several experimental and practical domains, including:</p>
      
      	<ul>
      		<li>Real-time data integrations for external information sources</li>
      		<li>Utility modules for automation and server interaction workflows</li>
      		<li>AI-driven conversational and task-oriented capabilities</li>
      		<li>Prototype systems for testing new features before broader deployment</li>
      	</ul>
      
      	<h2>How to Use Mico</h2>
      
      	<p>
      		Invite Mico to your Discord server and start exploring its capabilities directly inside your community.
      	</p>
      
      	<a
      		href="https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=1230073861580783647"
      		target="_blank"
      		rel="noopener noreferrer"
      	>
      		Add Mico to Discord
      	</a>
      
      	<p>
      		After installation, use <code>/help</code> inside your server to explore available commands,
      		features, and usage guidelines.
      	</p>
      
      	<h2>Why Mico</h2>
      
      	<p>
      		Mico is designed as an engineering-first system: lightweight in structure, flexible in design,
      		and continuously evolving through experimentation rather than static planning.
      	</p>
      
      	<p>
      		It exists to shorten the gap between idea and implementation, turning Discord into a functional
      		development environment for real-time system testing.
      	</p>
      
      	<p>
      		For governance and usage boundaries, refer to the
      		<a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      	</p>
      </main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>